<title>TAIWAN: Taiwan's grain import value up sharply in August.</title>
<headline>Taiwan's grain import value up sharply in August.</headline>
<dateline>TAIPEI 1996-09-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>The value of Taiwan's grain and oilseed imports in August was US$291.6 million, up 40.7 percent from $207.2 million in August 1995, Finance Ministry figures showed.</p>
<p>Taiwan traders attributed the rise in grain import values to the rise of international prices from the same period a year ago. Total August tonnages were not available.</p>
<p>The following is a table of major grain import figures in millions of U.S. dollars:</p>
<p>			    August 1996     August 1995</p>
<p> Wheat			    17.7	  16.2</p>
<p> Corn			    123.9	  63.0</p>
<p> Soybeans			 74.9	  70.5</p>
<p>--Taipei Newsroom (2-5080815)</p>
</text>
